 ### [Surface-based Instancing with Noise Modulation](1582-surface-based-instancing-with-noise-modulation.md)
-Generates high-density point clouds from surface primitives to achieve smooth volumetric appearance at high resolutions. It differs from the base method by explicitly instantiating a massive number of points (e.g., ~400 million) per primitive and modulating their density or position using procedural noise functions before rasterization or voxelization [1582-surface-based-instancing-with-noise-modulation.md].
