 ### [WebGL 2 Hardware Instancing](3152-webgl-2-hardware-instancing.md)
-Sends a single base primitive (typically a 2x2x2 cube) to the GPU and executes `gl.drawElementsInstanced` to render hundreds of thousands of copies simultaneously. It solves the CPU bottleneck associated with issuing individual draw calls for large numbers of voxels by packing translation, scaling, and color data into flat typed arrays. Unlike surface-based instancing which modulates geometry with noise, this method relies on explicit instance buffers and procedural sampling (e.g., from heightmaps) to dictate vertex positions and colors.
