-### Sphere Impostors for DEM Pebbles
-Rendering of Discrete Element Method (DEM) pebble beds using instanced sphere impostors. Each pebble is drawn as a quad with an exact orthographic ray-sphere hit test in the fragment shader, providing sphere shading and depth [S2, unofficial]. Draw instanced quads: For each pebble, submit an instance of a quad geometry. The shader performs an exact orthographic ray-sphere intersection test per fragment [S2, unofficial]. Render to offscreen target: Draw the impostors into an offscreen target, which egui then displays. This allows interaction (orbit, zoom) while positions stream [S2, unofficial]. Scale: 27,000 pebbles are rendered at interactive rates [S2, unofficial]. CPU Overhead: Submitting a frame takes 1.2-1.3 ms of CPU time [S2, unofficial]. Fallback: If no wgpu device is available, egui discs are used as the fallback rendering method [S2, unofficial].
